/*!
\page page_stPhmdHit StPhmdHit

\brief Single pad-cell hit in the STAR Photon Multiplicity Detector (PHMD/PMD).

\section phmdHit_overview Overview

StPhmdHit stores the raw signal from one cell of the STAR PHMD (Photon
Multiplicity Detector) which covers forward rapidity 2.3 < η < 3.9.  The
detector consists of two planes: PMD (photon detection, behind lead converter)
and CPV (charged-particle veto, in front of lead).  Each plane has 12
supermodules containing a honeycomb-cell pad array.

A hit records the supermodule, sub-detector (PMD or CPV), cell row and
column, the raw ADC count, and the calibrated energy deposition.

\section phmdHit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StPhmdHit
\endcode

Owned by \ref page_stPhmdModule "StPhmdModule" inside
\ref page_stPhmdDetector "StPhmdDetector".

\section phmdHit_members Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Int_t | mSuperModuleNumber | Global supermodule index [0, 11]. |
| Int_t | mSubDetector | 0 = PMD (photon), 1 = CPV (charged-particle veto). |
| Int_t | mRow | Cell row within the supermodule. |
| Int_t | mCol | Cell column within the supermodule. |
| Float_t | mEnergy | Calibrated energy deposit [GeV]. |
| Int_t | mAdc | Raw ADC count. |

\section phmdHit_methods Key Methods

- \c superModule() / \c module() — supermodule index.
- \c subDetector() — PMD or CPV plane.
- \c row() / \c column() — cell position.
- \c energy() — calibrated energy [GeV].
- \c adc() — raw ADC count.
- \c set*() — corresponding setters.

\section phmdHit_seealso See Also

\ref page_stPhmdCluster "StPhmdCluster",
\ref page_stPhmdModule "StPhmdModule",
\ref page_stPhmdDetector "StPhmdDetector"
*/
